Changes made in VyanLLM relative to AirLLM (based on AirLLM 4.0.0, October 2026):
- Renamed the package, modules and classes from airllm / AirLLM to vyanllm / VyanLLM.
- Prefetching works together with compression; dequantization runs on the device.
- Optional asynchronous host-to-GPU copies on a side CUDA stream (async_copy).
- Memory cleanup once per forward pass instead of after every layer (memory_cleanup).
- One-time conversion of wider-dtype shards to the runtime dtype (precast_shards).
- Layer cache that keeps layers in memory between tokens (cache_gb, gpu_cache_gb).
- Shard format selected per backend, so the PyTorch path works on macOS (Apple GPU / MPS).
- O(n) decompression of compressed shards; 8-bit no longer forces float16 output.
- Benchmark script comparing against the original (examples/benchmark.py).
- Removed the unrelated research projects, notebooks and assets bundled in the AirLLM repository.
